WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.787
This is a fictional teaching conversation in the continuing intake project.

00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:09.138
Learn Maya's role: she reviews summaries before they move forward.

00:00:09.138 --> 00:00:14.795
Invite the concern: what concerns you about the draft in your reviewing role?

00:00:14.795 --> 00:00:20.017
Maya says it could appear to be her professional wording before approval.

00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:23.498
Summarize what you heard, then test your understanding.

00:00:23.498 --> 00:00:30.461
When Maya adds attribution to the concern about accuracy, revise the summary and check it again.

00:00:30.461 --> 00:00:33.942
Explore support: what would help you examine that?

00:00:33.942 --> 00:00:38.728
She suggests one fictional editable draft with a visible approval step.

00:00:38.728 --> 00:00:46.126
Name what needs review: the service reviewer can prepare the example, while the manager reviews attribution rules.

00:00:46.126 --> 00:00:49.607
Simulated confirmation means the summary fits this rehearsal.

00:00:49.607 --> 00:00:52.218
It does not approve real use.
